1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,240
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,300
I play the Seal of Auriculcos!

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:10,580
Then I'll activate the Magic
Card, Full Armor Gravitation!

4
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:26,980
I'M INVINCIBLE!

5
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,140
My move!

6
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,480
Look out!

7
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,640
Now we're talking.

8
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,640
Let's see you stand up to this guy!

9
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:24,300
It's time to duel!

10
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,800
If I can't access Kaiba's
satellite, we'll never find Joey.

11
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:03,680
This has to work.

12
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,040
Access granted.

13
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:08,660
I got in, Grandpa.

14
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,000
Well done. Now what's it say?

15
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,940
I can't wait around anymore.

16
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:16,392
Joey needs our help, and he needs it now.

17
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,960
Tristan, you must chill. Tay is right.

18
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,897
Without Kaiba's tracking system,
we have no hope of finding it.

19
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:26,240
Am I the only one here who
understands what's going on?

20
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:29,560
Joey may be losing his
soul as we speak. Let's go!

21
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,824
I didn't think of it like that.

22
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,780
Maybe we should go. Not yet.

23
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:37,757
We have to have faith
that Rebecca can find him.

24
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,722
Until then, I know Joey
can take care of himself.

25
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:43,476
He's been in tough situations before.

26
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,880
Not this tough.

27
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:46,900
Hey, I did it!

28
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:48,255
I finally found Joey!

29
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,700
This readout's right.

30
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,520
Joey's not far, guys.

31
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:56,387
All right, I'll take
this and track him down.

32
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:58,397
You move the trailer to a safer place.

33
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,120
Not so fast, Pharaoh.

34
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:01,597
You're not going alone.

35
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,510
That's right.

36
00:03:02,593 --> 00:03:03,877
We're all in this together.

37
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,960
I guess you've made up your minds.

38
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:07,370
Thank you.

39
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,560
Now, let's go.

40
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,340
Rebecca, you stay here.

41
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,917
Duke, you keep an eye on
them until we get back.

42
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,830
You got it.

43
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,240
No, I want to go, too.

44
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:18,940
Come on, Grandpa.

45
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,126
We've got our own work to do.

46
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,124
We need your talents back here.

47
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:29,160
Rebecca, as soon as Joey's
safe, we'll find Yugi

48
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,460
Promise me he's all right

49
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:37,200
Yugi's going to be just fine,
I promise Please, trust me

50
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:43,300
Come on, you don't have a second to lose
So go kick some butt and take names Well,

51
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,280
that's one way to put
it Let's chit-chat later

52
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:52,500
Good luck with everything You too
If you need us, just call Right

53
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,180
Don't worry, Rebecca.

54
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,294
Yugi will be back here safe
and sound in no time at all.

55
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,900
But how do you know?

56
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:04,220
Because I believe in the Pharaoh.

57
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,680
And you should, too. Fine.

58
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:12,137
Rebecca's having a hard time forgiving
the Pharaoh for what happened to Yugi.

59
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:14,926
She must think he'll be
tempted by evil again.

60
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,947
Let's just hope she's wrong.

61
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:22,625
You gonna stare at that
card all night, are ya?

62
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,580
You know,

63
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:30,817
it works better when you actually
play it You're even dumber than

64
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:36,940
you look But you asked for it First
I summon my Brigadier of Landstar

65
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:45,217
And then I activate my
Monster Reborn card And

66
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,888
I'm using it to bring
my Rocket Warrior back

67
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:54,240
And finally, I play this!

68
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,120
The Claw of Hermos!

69
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,460
About time.

70
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,033
I was waiting for that.

71
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:08,792
This way, I can really prove my strength.

72
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,300
So go, use your dragon!

73
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,960
No monster's too strong for my armor!

74
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,420
How far is Joey?

75
00:05:18,020 --> 00:05:20,300
Just a few blocks according to this.

76
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,177
I just hope I'm reading this thing right.

77
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:24,160
Don't say that!

78
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:27,500
Hold on, guys.

79
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,720
Joey must have played his dragon.

80
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:40,540
Now I'll merge my claw of
hammos with my rocket warrior.

81
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,180
What's that?

82
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,220
My Rocket Hamos Cannon!

83
00:05:56,640 --> 00:06:00,860
It's the perfect item to help my
Brigadier of Landstar take you down!

84
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,837
You're kidding me, right?

85
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:09,277
That puny little guy couldn't
even put a dent in my armor!

86
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,237
He's not looking to make a dent!

87
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,977
He's gonna blow the whole thing away!

88
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:18,140
Now, Brigadier of Landstar,
attack with Rocket Hammo's cannon!

89
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:27,717
Danger.

90
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,447
Opponent attack unavoidable.

91
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:33,060
Probability of armor destruction 100%.

92
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,280
Guess it worked!

93
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:47,931
That cannon should have blown
the armor right off his back!

94
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,470
Vingo!

95
00:06:52,553 --> 00:06:53,383
I win!

96
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:56,402
Looks like I'm the last
man standing, right, pal?

97
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,390
Wrong.

98
00:06:59,473 --> 00:07:00,303
No way!

99
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:05,920
I may be down, but I'm not
out, thanks to my armor.

100
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:07,270
But how?

101
00:07:07,353 --> 00:07:08,800
I destroyed your armor.

102
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,277
It's got special abilities, remember?

103
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:16,180
And when you destroyed it just now,
you let loose its most devastating one!

104
00:07:22,220 --> 00:07:25,020
Don't you hate always
being one step behind me?

105
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,840
I know you're bluffing.

106
00:07:28,040 --> 00:07:30,557
You have nothing left
and you're about to lose.

107
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,470
Now go!

108
00:07:31,553 --> 00:07:32,383
Not quite.

109
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:36,260
I'm still holding my Databrain
magic card. Oh, right.

110
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:39,997
It activated when you destroyed my armor.

111
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:42,540
What's it doing in my racket, Cannon?

112
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:44,540
What does it look like?

113
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:46,460
It's absorbing information.

114
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,520
As we speak,

115
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:54,200
my data brain is memorizing the precise
molecular structure of your cannon. Why?

116
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:01,440
So it can create an exact duplicate of
your weapon on my side of the field.

117
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,160
But I'm not done yet.

118
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,420
Say hello to an old friend.

119
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:08,717
You remember my card that
never goes away, don't you?

120
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:11,160
If not, this'll jog your memory.

121
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,260
Psychic Armahead, return!

122
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:22,540
And since you're so happy to see it,
I'll also play another Burning Knuckle.

123
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,140
Just because I like you.

124
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,904
But this time, things are
going to be different.

125
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:31,857
Because I'm upgrading my
armor with a new weapon.

126
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:34,411
It's the one I just got from you, Wheeler.

127
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,780
How could I ever repay you?

128
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,620
Wait a sec, I think I know.

129
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:42,300
I'll use it on you.

130
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:43,840
Eh, no thank you.

131
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,100
I insist!

132
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,660
Rocket Hammo's cannon attack!

133
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,320
Oh, no.

134
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,100
It's fading.

135
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:09,870
Wheeler.

136
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:17,076
Lucky for you, this rocket
cannon only lasts one turn.

137
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:19,080
But by the looks of you,

138
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,737
I think one turn was all I needed
to knock you down for the count.

139
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:25,232
So I guess this means I win the duel, eh?

140
00:09:27,560 --> 00:09:30,200
Joey, Wheeler never gives up.

141
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:31,750
What?

142
00:09:31,833 --> 00:09:32,997
Look at yourself, mate.

143
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,910
You're a mess.

144
00:09:33,993 --> 00:09:35,801
So walk away while you still can.

145
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,260
No way.

146
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:43,001
Hey, I'm doing this for Mai, because whether
she knows it or not, she needs my help.

147
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:47,540
And in order to do that, I need to win.

148
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,720
This guy's even tougher than I thought.

149
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:56,004
I've never faced an opponent with
this much determination before.

150
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:01,988
After what I put him through,
he should have given up by now.

151
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:06,700
Time to take control of
this duel, so look out!

152
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:09,700
There's too much at stake for me to lose.

153
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:16,500
You're mine, Wheeler.

154
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,720
I like this one. Fine.

155
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:26,337
We don't have any time
to shop around anyway.

156
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:27,540
Get in, Mokuba.

157
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,760
Let's pay darts a visit.

158
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,220
Sounds good to me.

159
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:33,960
What's going on here?

160
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:35,937
What are you two doing in this car?

161
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:39,620
What do you think we're
doing? We're buying it. What?

162
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:42,500
I don't have time to
play games, young man.

163
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,680
I think this should cover it.

164
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,940
Keep the change.

165
00:10:47,420 --> 00:10:48,660
Get back here.

166
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,280
There goes my job.

167
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:56,640
Or maybe not.

168
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:00,620
Great idea.

169
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:02,314
Beat's taking the bus.

170
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,040
I have a feeling
Wheeler's in trouble again

171
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:12,680
But I don't have time to bail that chump
out I have bigger things to deal with

172
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:28,240
Too weak to make a move?

173
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:32,620
I don't think so I play this
face down and end my turn.

174
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:37,357
So I guess you couldn't find a monster
that was strong enough to take me down.

175
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:40,077
That means your life
points are wide open, mate.

176
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,597
And I've got just the
thing to help me smash

177
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:45,520
them to smithereens and
end this duel already.

178
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:47,760
Here goes.

179
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,800
I summon my black hole
shield in attack mode.

180
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:02,217
this gives my burning
knuckle 200 extra attack

181
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:07,437
points scanning opponent's
playing field monster cards

182
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:12,597
zero face down cards one
say goodbye to the rest

183
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:16,100
of your life points wheeler
burning Big Knuckle, attack!

184
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,620
With Iron Fist Uppercut!

185
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,300
It's all over!

186
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,020
No way!

187
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:33,785
You thought you were the only one
with a space suit, didn't you?

188
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:38,880
Well, you activated my
Aura Armor Trap Card!

189
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,628
You're gonna be kidding me!

190
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:43,480
Detecting rival armor.

191
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,757
And I decided the only way to beat
you was to fight armor with armor.

192
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:52,797
You see, when Aura Armor is on the
field and I get attacked, it activates.

193
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,880
If I have under 2,000 life points.

194
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:58,037
Sure, I had to give up half of those
life points in order to use it.

195
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:01,944
But as an added bonus, I was able
to cancel out your last attack.

196
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:04,160
And get this snazzy suit.

197
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,757
Why don't you try something original, huh?

198
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:09,720
Because nobody likes a
wannabe. Don't worry.

199
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:11,317
My armor's different than yours.

200
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:15,837
Mine is directly linked to my life
points, so when it gets destroyed, I lose.

201
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,797
So how's that for original, huh?

202
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:18,900
Now let's go.

203
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:20,770
I see.

204
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:22,999
One more round and one more attack.

205
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:25,280
Last man standing wins the duel.

206
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,630
I'm in.

207
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:29,080
I lay one card face down.

208
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:35,427
Joey must have summoned
his legendary dragon.

209
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,340
That's why mine was glowing.

210
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,540
But why did the light fade?

211
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,020
My move!

212
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:46,180
Come on! Bingo!

213
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:48,260
Now check this out!

214
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:50,560
I activate Roll of Fate!

215
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,880
Here's how it works!

216
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:58,717
Whatever number the die lands on,
I get to pick up that many cards!

217
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,918
But I also have to send that
many cards to the grave!

218
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:04,700
Yes! Four!

219
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:13,840
What's this bloke up to?

220
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:17,300
All right, I'm gonna start
things off with this.

221
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:20,400
The magic card, Red-Eyes Transmigration.

222
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:25,600
All I have to do is sacrifice my
Red-Eyes Black Dragon, and you're done.

223
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,580
It's that simple.

224
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,900
He's not even on the field.

225
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,660
But he's in my hand.

226
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:36,540
So I sacrifice my Red-Eyes Black
Dragon and my new armor card,

227
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:38,660
so I can play War of the Red.

228
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:00,100
What in the world?

229
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,830
Yeah!

230
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:07,079
What do you think?

231
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:09,495
I know, you need a closer look, right?

232
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,240
Lord of the Red, attack!

233
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,060
There's no way out this time!

234
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,720
That's what you think!

235
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:28,060
Go, Black Hole Shield!

236
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:33,300
Hey, what's going on?

237
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,800
Your attack failed.

238
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:43,400
By sacrificing my shield, I protected
my life points from any damage.

239
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:45,130
No!

240
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,398
I thought my strategy was foolproof.

241
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:49,960
Oh, well, guess not.

242
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,840
I saved myself, but barely.

243
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:55,900
Oh, look at me.

244
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:56,960
I'm shaking.

245
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:00,397
That's never happened to
me during a battle before.

246
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:03,160
This guy's pushing me
to my dueling limits.

247
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:05,920
Come to think of it,

248
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:10,820
this could be the greatest challenge
I've ever faced You know what, Wheeler?

249
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:16,560
I gotta admit, you're putting up quite
a fight You do, but you know what, pal?

250
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:21,620
I'm not fighting for fun This
is about saving my friends

251
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,160
Hey, Ma,

252
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:30,717
you're just in time to
catch the end of the

253
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,420
greatest duel ever played You
and I had a deal, remember?

254
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:36,240
Joey Wheeler's mine!

255
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,120
Mine, no!

256
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:42,817
Look, you've done enough, so why don't
you take a hike and let me finish this?

257
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,260
Sorry, no can do.

258
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,760
I'm having way too much
fun out here to stop now.

259
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:52,400
Plus, this duel is no
place for you. Why's that?

260
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,740
There's too much at stake.

261
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:57,837
I won't let you risk
losing everything you have.

262
00:16:57,920 --> 00:17:00,857
That's why I challenged
Wheeler in the first place.

263
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:01,960
To protect you.

264
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:06,697
I wanted to get rid of him so you'd
be able to move on with your life.

265
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:09,133
And that's exactly what I'm going to do.

266
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,080
Guess what?

267
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:13,321
I'm fighting for the same reason.

268
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:15,157
Then let's get on with it.

269
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:17,534
I can't wait to see what you play next.

270
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:20,640
You're going to have to wait, pal,

271
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:23,740
because I play one card
face down and end my turn.

272
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,540
Big mistake, pal.

273
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:31,077
I activate Monster Reborn,
which lets me bring back...

274
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,540
Bust a pile!

275
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:44,500
Here comes the last attack
of the duel, Wheeler!

276
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,820
Not quite! I have this!

277
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:50,180
I activate my scapegoat magic card!

278
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:53,460
Oh, come on!

279
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,580
How's Pipsqueaks can't
block my fist of iron?

280
00:17:56,760 --> 00:18:00,137
Well, it's a good thing that's not
what I'm trying to do, isn't it?

281
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:01,050
Huh?

282
00:18:01,133 --> 00:18:02,040
What are you up to?

283
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:09,980
My armor's got a special power, too.

284
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:13,517
Lord of the Red is able to
automatically destroy every other

285
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:17,659
monster on the field whenever two
magic cards are played in one turn.

286
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,200
How long?

287
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,400
Two cards?

288
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,740
But you only played one card.

289
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:28,060
True, but you played Monster Reborn, which
counts as the second magic card I needed.

290
00:18:28,260 --> 00:18:29,090
No!

291
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:34,660
I don't believe this.

292
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,820
I know you're fluffing, Wheeler.

293
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:42,920
There's no way your armor can beat mine.

294
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:13,260
Still think I was bluffing?

295
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:21,780
My arm is gone, but I still
have a few life points left.

296
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,740
So this duel's still on.

297
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,294
Come on, give me everything you've got.

298
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,040
If you say so. Here goes.

299
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,840
It's been nice knowing you.

300
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,980
Not so fast.

301
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,260
Activate trap.

302
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:42,100
Extinction fist.

303
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,357
This card allows me to
neutralize your attack right

304
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:48,616
on the spot and rid the field
of your Lord of the Red.

305
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,040
Go, extinction fist.

306
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,380
It was a good echo.

307
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:11,160
Unfortunately for you, I
was one step ahead. Again!

308
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,040
Well, I gotta hand it to you, pal.

309
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:19,160
I didn't see that one coming.

310
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,480
Well, that was the point.

311
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:34,980
This is it.

312
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:37,612
They're both one attack away from defeat.

313
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:42,260
In the next round, one of them's going
to be trapped by the seal forever.
